                <pb facs="0640" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg634"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. von Holleben to
                        Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: Acting under
                    instructions from my Government, and in order to settle the legal tender
                    question in Samoa, I have the honor to suggest to you that our Tepresentatives
                    in Apia shall be directed to inform the Samoan Government that the exclusion of
                    German coin is against the Samoan treaty, and that German coin must be admitted
                    into Samoa just as well as United States and British coin, 20 marks to be taken
                    as worth $4.76.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Holleben.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
